  "core_question": "What analyses must a rural community hospital board conduct across clinical, legal, and financial domains when converting to for-profit, selling its real estate via sale‑leaseback, and spinning out a charitable foundation holding the proceeds?",
  "rationale": "The transaction involves clinical service continuity, complex nonprofit-to-for-profit conversion and tax-exempt status issues, and intricate financing/valuation considerations that each specialist can address.",
  "routes": ["healthcare", "legal", "finance"],
  "sub_questions": {
    "healthcare": "What are the key clinical considerations a rural 90‑bed hospital must evaluate when transitioning from nonprofit to for-profit status, including impacts on patient care quality, workforce retention, community benefit obligations, and compliance with CMS regulations?",
    "legal": "What are the primary legal issues a board must address when converting a nonprofit community hospital to for-profit, executing a sale‑leaseback of its real estate, and spinning out a charitable foundation that holds transaction proceeds, particularly regarding IRS 501(c)(3) status, fiduciary duties, state statutes, and lease structure?",
    "finance": "What financial analyses should the board conduct to evaluate the feasibility and value of converting the hospital to for-profit, selling its real estate in a sale‑leaseback, and establishing a charitable foundation holding the proceeds, including valuation, financing terms, tax implications, cash flow projections, and return on investment?"
  },
  "requires_recency_disclosure": true,
  "recency_notes": "IRS 501(c)(3) sale‑leaseback guidance post‑2024, recent state nonprofit conversion statutes, and evolving private equity deal structures in healthcare."
}
